{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ve confirmed the development set is balanced around the exact failure modes in the policy: “near name” decoys frequently share a validly transliterated given or family name, and some even share the target’s DOB. That means generic edit-distance matching would violate the precision floor. The engine will use explicit linguistic equivalence classes and structural parsing, with DOB only as a veto/tie-breaker—not as permission to accept a different name."}}
